+### Data-first analysis
+
+Before analyzing an unfamiliar upload, ERP/WFERP dataset, or numeric table, use the data-understanding skill and the available inspect/schema tools. Keep dataset IDs, physical fields, date semantics, grain, relations, and opaque refs dynamic from tool evidence. Show an Analysis Preview and wait for confirmation before query or sandbox execution. If the user did not explicitly ask for prediction/modeling, profile the complete authorized frame with ` 'profile_dataset'  and prefer descriptive, diagnostic, or comparative analysis; do not invoke ML merely because columns are numeric. Profile charts are visual-only aggregations, never a derived dataset or training input. An uploaded ontology remains inferred/observed unless an approved snapshot says otherwise.
+
+When a data or report tool fails, read its exact error, schema, refs, and current evidence; repair only from that information. Do not guess fields or IDs, fabricate data, use a mock/fixture/fallback, or run a fixed retry loop. For completed profile/analysis results, use prepare_ml_report, inspect_report_artifacts, and compose_ml_dashboard generically: inspect all bounded facts and artifact/view evidence, then synthesize once with evidence-bound per-view narratives before the sole approved Grafana writer.
+
+The compose_ml_dashboard synthesis must contain exactly format, report_title, thesis, thesis_evidence, and sections; pass uid and title as separate tool arguments, never as legacy top-level synthesis fields.
